                    insight_delivered:      `Transformation delivered: you ran it as a coordinated change — platform-first to hit the mandate, reskilling funded right behind, value-based coverage, a channel-neutral commission plan and pricing governance set before the marketplace opened. Revenue retained, adoption up, capability built, and a payback the CFO can defend.`,
                    insight_stranded:       `Platform stranded: you funded the technology and starved the people. The punch-out catalogue is live but adoption sits near 9%, reps protect their commission, and the £2.4M platform is a tool nobody uses. Technology and capability had to be sequenced together.`,
                    insight_short:          `You didn't fully reconcile the levers. Technology, capability and operating-model still tell slightly different stories — enough for the mandate, the rep council or the CFO to find the seam.`,
                    insight_account:        `You lost the £9M anchor account. A hard customer deadline treated as a target — a slipped integration, no field-led task-force — triggered the switching clause, and a second mandate wave is now in motion.`,
                    insight_pricewar:       `You started a price war with yourself: a marketplace opened below field list price with no governance rule, so your largest accounts now demand the same discount on millions of spend. The channel you opened to win volume erodes the margin you had.`,
                    insight_capability:     `Rep capability stayed low: too little reskilling and change investment, or a commission plan that punished the reps you needed. Training is content; enablement is tools, coaching and behaviour change — and only enablement shifts what reps actually do.`,
                    insight_adoption:       `Digital adoption stalled: customers and reps aren't using what you built. Adoption follows incentives and enablement, not platform features — without the people change, the technology investment never converts.`,
                    insight_governed:       `Channel and margin risk are low — coverage matched to account value, incentives aligned, and a pricing floor set before any channel opened. That is channel conflict governed before it erupted, which is what protected your margin.`,

                    hint_stranded:          `Your platform is stranded — funded technology, starved people. Pour the remaining budget into reskilling and enablement, or adoption never leaves single digits.`,
                    hint_pricewar:          `You've opened a channel below field list price. Set a pricing-governance floor now, before your largest accounts demand the same discount on millions of spend.`,
                    hint_account:           `The £9M anchor account is at the switching clause. Send a field-led task-force to finish the integration — service and integration win it back, not a discount.`,
                    hint_adoption:          `Adoption is stuck near the start line. The fix is enablement and a channel-neutral incentive, not more platform features — change what reps and customers are rewarded for.`,
